[candidate · 11:44] Let me back into the bean line, since we weren't given it directly.

Two years ago COGS was 42 index units. Beans at 25% of that is 10.5. Everything else — dairy, packaging, food — is 31.5.

Other inputs up 37.5%: 31.5 × 1.375 = 43.3.

Current total COGS I calculated at 66.7. So beans today = 66.7 − 43.3 = 23.4.

That's 10.5 to 23.4 — up about 123%, more than doubling. And beans have gone from 25% of COGS to roughly 35%.

So the ranking is clear. Coffee beans are the single largest driver; other inputs at 37.5% are a real secondary issue but roughly a third the impact. Both are running far ahead of the 15% revenue growth, which says we absorbed input inflation without passing it through.

That's the question I want to close out: have we taken any menu price increases in the past two years?
